@using System.Globalization
@* Shared "Your Formation" output: rendered by the Academy SSR page AND the
   /api/academy/formation Datastar endpoint via RazorRenderer so the two can
   never drift apart. The root element carries the id the SSE patch targets. *@
<div class="lesson lesson-output" id="formation-output">
    <h3>Your leader's preferred mix</h3>
    <p class="lesson-math"><strong>@(Result.RInf.ToString("0.0%", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) infantry / @(Result.RCav.ToString("0.0%", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) cavalry / @(Result.RArc.ToString("0.0%", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)) archers</strong></p>
    <p>Archers hit hardest per troop, so they always get the biggest share.</p>
    <div class="lesson-fact">
        @(Result.ArcherScarce
            ? "You don't have enough archers for that mix. Send all your archers, 5k infantry, and fill the rest with cavalry."
            : "Your troops fit the mix. Scale each type to match the leader's share.")
    </div>
    <h3>Send this per march</h3>
    <p class="lesson-math"><strong>@FmtK(Result.RecInf) infantry / @FmtK(Result.RecCav) cavalry / @FmtK(Result.RecArc) archers</strong>&nbsp;(cap @(Result.Cap <= 0 ? "uncapped" : FmtK(Result.Cap)), @Result.Q simultaneous rallies)</p>
    <p>Each march scores about @(Result.PerMarchDmg.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture)); all @Result.Q simultaneous rallies together &asymp; <strong>@(Result.TotalDmg.ToString("N0", CultureInfo.InvariantCulture))</strong>. (Scores are for comparing setups. Not real damage numbers.)</p>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public AcademyFormation.Result Result { get; set; } = null!;
}
